      "passage_sha256": "25ee7a20c884284dd453d8f76615707b0d810ba21616fd74ec907feb7ffcbef8",
      "ending": "A fresh primary search found the stronger [Gan–Liu–Wu v1, *Lebesgue measure of distance sets and L² ball inflation*](https://arxiv.org/html/2610.05015v1), submitted October 4, 2026. Its full proof text was read through the weighted estimate's ending (text lines 1–1122), including the profile structure lemma, finite-scale subdivisions, all three inflation steps and final mass summation. It uses finite-scale profile regularization, not a fixed regular subset. For alpha=dim_H E and beta=dim_P E it states positivity when",
