    {
      "local": "frontier/sources/i136_birational_positivity_discovery/context-reading.txt",
      "start": 1268,
      "end": 1295,
      "line_count": 4499,
      "file_sha256": "237080a7c5e842845d5cfc6946f0abc9241f8d2613b2a5d2f8089476e8c0857e",
      "passage_sha256": "a81a43994c23aeb291acab1bfd8da497415e71fc8430ce7b3ee0eaf980c135ca",
      "ending": "**F10 — PASS.** Differentiating S and commuting Lambda produces both terms as written. **F11 — PASS.** The flat-coordinate multi-index product formula and `nabla_i(J/r)=r^-1(nabla_i-f_i)J` are exact; a covariant word uses all ordered subwords and acquires curvature upon reordering. **F12 — PASS.** Differentiation includes s, both kernel variables, the Jacobi field, profile-radius derivative, frame, physical normal, traction coefficients and area. Repetition retains `s^-1` times ordered conjugated derivatives. The source's six trace derivatives, five coefficient derivatives and seven profile derivatives fit its eight-profile allowance; a new energy would owe any additional orders. Neither known cutoff region proves the unmatched-core estimate.",
      "convention": "splitlines; LF joined without appended LF"
    },
    {
      "local": "frontier/sources/i136_birational_positivity_discovery/context-reading.txt",
      "start": 1451,
      "end": 1710,
      "line_count": 4499,
      "file_sha256": "237080a7c5e842845d5cfc6946f0abc9241f8d2613b2a5d2f8089476e8c0857e",
      "passage_sha256": "c88200501a1b32ead5581fe3cbda4cb94b8610639861bb69587be03fdd330179",
      "ending": "**Small-ball family and balanced graph, (3.1)–(3.3): PASS without repairs.** On each fixed finite set of Sobolev and parameter orders the pulled-back physical Dirichlet inverse is uniformly bounded down to zero radius. Its limiting operator is the constant Lamé operator, not the scalar Laplacian. Differentiating that inverse controls the smoothing remainder as well as the boundary symbol. Hence `B_r=r T_B`, `F_r=Lambda^-1 B_r` have the asserted orders and smooth parameter dependence. The identity-plus-positive operator `M_r=I+F_r^*F_r` is invertible on L2; ellipticity and regularity extend this to each fixed Sobolev scale. With `G_r g=(g,F_r g)`, `Pi_r=G_r M_r^-1 G_r^*` is exactly the orthogonal graph projection. The orthogonal complement is `(-F_r^*a,a)`. Undoing balancing gives the original graph and annihilator, with bilinear transposes for evaluation and Hermitian adjoints only for norms. Parameter bounds after substituting the profile allow powers of beta. They are not unweighted center derivative bounds. The output factor `R=diag(I3,r)` produces the displayed unscaled lower-left `r^-1`; the test `g=omega` verifies that this loss is real.",
      "convention": "splitlines; LF joined without appended LF"
    },
